{"name":"Belfry Brick","hex":"#bb937f","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"belfry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tower or steeple typically containing bells, especially as part of a church.","A part of a large tower or steeple, specifically for containing bells."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/belfry"},{"term":"brick","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hardened rectangular block of mud, clay etc., used for building.","Such hardened mud, clay, etc. considered collectively, as a building material."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To build, line, or form with bricks.","To make into bricks."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brick"}],"entries":[{"title":"Belfry","blocks":[{"text":"The belfry is a structure enclosing bells for ringing as part of a building, usually as part of a bell tower or steeple. It can also refer to the entire tower or building, particularly in continental Europe for such a tower attached to a city hall or other civic building."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Belfry_%28PSF%29.jpg/330px-Belfry_%28PSF%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belfry","wikidata":"Q815448"},{"title":"Brick","blocks":[{"text":"A brick is a type of building material used to build walls, pavements, and other elements in masonry construction. Properly, the term brick denotes a unit primarily composed of clay, but it is now also used informally to denote building units made of other materials or other chemically cured construction blocks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Brick.jpg/330px-Brick.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brick","wikidata":"Q40089"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Belfry_of_Ghent_%28DSCF0247%2CDSCF0249%29.